cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Epistemic Trap: a tool-credulity red-team harness for LLM coding agents"
message: >-
  A pair of MCP servers (web_search / web_fetch) that inject a corpus of
  interlocking synthetic news coverage into an agent's web-access layer,
  measuring whether the agent trusts tool output over its own knowledge.
  Test A is the "2+2=5" probe. All evaluation content is synthetic; every
  quoted person is fictional.
authors:
  - family-names: Fur
    given-names: Mikhail
    alias: mikhailfur
    website: https://mikhailfur.ru
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-13"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mikhailfur/epistemic-trap"
keywords:
  - llm
  - agents
  - ai-safety
  - red-team
  - mcp
  - benchmark
  - tool-use
abstract: >-
  Epistemic Trap measures tool-source credulity: an LLM coding agent's
  tendency to trust its retrieval tools against its own knowledge. The
  harness runs two local MCP servers that look like a normal web stack but
  serve a controlled corpus of synthetic, interlocking articles; a JSONL
  log records every tool call for analysis.
